$build = @'
CODEX BUILD (22 Oct 2026, desk plan/03). The generic text appended AFTER this brief says branch from origin/master: THAT IS WRONG FOR THIS JOB. Master is about 1100 commits behind what ships. Your base is origin/claude/rel-20261022m (the installed Civil 3.0.70 / Manager 1.1.70 line; run git fetch origin first) unless the task says Structural, then origin/claude/rel-20261022s2. Everything else in the appended text (own worktree under a SHORT path, merge never rebase, REGRESSION_LOG.md entry at the top keeping both sides, build and test rules, no secrets, plain-English UI) DOES apply. Read C:\TimOS\RULES.md first. BUILD AND TEST: foreground, ALWAYS with -p:SkipDevBundle=true -nr:false --disable-build-servers and the AutoCAD reference parameters in C:\CE_PLAN\areas\release-v3-colleagues-TRAIN_C57_ASSEMBLY_REPORT_2026-10-20.md (net10 and net48 builds; test totals must be in the thousands). NEVER deploy: never build without SkipDevBundle, never write under the AutoCAD ApplicationPlugins folder or ProgramData, never touch Tim's settings files, never start AutoCAD. Defaults of existing switches do not change; any NEW behaviour that changes what a drafter sees ships behind a Settings switch OFF. DELIVER: a branch and a DRAFT pull request against the base, plus an ANSWER FIRST report file in C:\CE_PLAN\areas (PR number, head, tests added, totals, what Tim will see, and the exact real-AutoCAD check) pushed by name from C:\CE_PLAN. END with a summary under 100 words.
