$builds = @(
 @('cx_b01_automation_ids', "TASK: TESTABILITY. Add AutomationProperties.AutomationId and AutomationProperties.Name (plain English, stable, unique within the window) to every interactive control of the key CE WPF windows so a UI Automation test can find and press them without pictures: Edit source, Edit Pipe, Edit Pit, Edit 2 Pipes, New Pit, Settings CDS (tabs, every checkbox and button, Save/Cancel), Checks palette (tabs, Show where, Check again, Close), What CE Found, X-Civil import (all tabs, Choose DWG, Read source, Import to drawing, Close), About, Help Centre. PURELY ADDITIVE: no layout, wording, colour or behaviour change. Add one test that walks each window type and fails if an interactive control has an empty AutomationId. Branch cx/automation-ids-c60. Report C:\CE_PLAN\areas\CODEX_BUILD_AUTOMATION_IDS_22OCT.md. Do not touch the Edit source window files that PR #1522 changes unless a one-line attribute is all that is needed."),
 @('cx_b02_test_state', "TASK: A READ-ONLY TEST COMMAND for the test runner. Add a Civil command CE_TEST_STATE (hidden from the ribbon, not in help) that, ONLY when the Settings switch testing.stateCommand is ON (default OFF; add its Settings row on the Advanced tab without making any tab taller than 670 px: the 150 percent fit test must stay green), prints ONE line of JSON to the command line and the CE log: DBMOD, UNDOCTL, UNDOMARKS, the count of selected entities and their handles (implied selection), whether a CE project record exists and its entity counts (pits, pipes), the last 3 CE command outcomes, the installed Civil/Manager/Structural versions. It must not open a transaction that writes, set a variable, change selection, or add an undo step (prove with a test). Purpose: the machine test runner reads this to assert undo/redo and record state after a pick or double-click (BUG-861). Branch cx/test-state-c60. Report C:\CE_PLAN\areas\CODEX_BUILD_TEST_STATE_22OCT.md."),
 @('cx_b03_outcome_struct_mgr', "TASK: COMMAND OUTCOME LINES FOR STRUCTURAL AND MANAGER. Civil writes one INFO line per command: 'Command outcome: <CMD> completed|cancelled|refused|failed N ms' (read #1507 in the C-60 line and the open fix for its semantics in the PR list: gh pr list --state open --search outcome). Build the same for Structural commands (CSREOBAR, CEMEMBER, SBEAM, LBUH, LBH, CEHATCHCHANGE, CEHATCHAUDIT and the rest in the Structural command registry) on base origin/claude/rel-20261022s2, and for Manager commands (CE_VERSION and the rest) on base origin/claude/rel-20261022m, one draft PR each (branches cx/outcome-struct and cx/outcome-mgr), behind the same Settings switch name and default as Civil, using the same line format so desk_jobs\\log_outcomes.ps1 reads them. A command that places or changes something and ends by Esc is 'completed'; nothing done = 'cancelled'; CE says no = 'refused'. Tests: the registry covers every [CommandMethod]. Report C:\CE_PLAN\areas\CODEX_BUILD_OUTCOME_STRUCT_MGR_22OCT.md."),
 @('cx_b04_guard_tests', "TASK: GUARD TESTS FOR THE CLASS OF DEFECT UNIT TESTS MISSED. Read C:\CE_PLAN\areas\AUDIT_C58_C60_S40_S41_2026-10-22.md and CODEX_AUDIT_*_22OCT.md (if present). Write source-pin / reflection guard tests (the repo already has this pattern: grep for tests named *Guard* and *SourcePin*) that fail when: (1) code reads the implied selection (SelectImplied) inside a CommandWillStart handler without a fallback or a log line; (2) a read-only command (list the read-only commands from the REGRESSION_LOG and the command card names: Checks, Tidy-labels preview, outcome logging, CDCHECKIGNORE with switch OFF) calls StartTransaction with write intent, SetValue, AppendEntity or a Dictionary write before its switch check; (3) code sets Linetype/Color on an EXISTING layer table record (bug 864); (4) a new Settings key is read without a documented default. Keep them targeted so they pass on the C-60 line today where the code is already right, and list in the report the places they flag (they may legitimately fail on known defects: mark those with a skip reason naming the BUG id). Branch cx/guard-tests-c60. Report C:\CE_PLAN\areas\CODEX_BUILD_GUARD_TESTS_22OCT.md."),
 @('cx_b05_sandbox_install', "TASK: CLEAN-PC INSTALL DRY RUN FOR 9 NOV. Windows 11 Pro has Windows Sandbox (feature Containers-DisposableClientVM). Investigate WITHOUT changing system settings (do not enable features, do not install anything on this PC): check whether the feature is enabled (Get-WindowsOptionalFeature -Online -FeatureName Containers-DisposableClientVM); write a PowerShell script C:\CE_PLAN\desk_jobs\scripts\clean_pc_install_dryrun.ps1 and a .wsb sandbox config that, when run by the desk on a PC where the feature is enabled, installs the Civil + Manager colleague installer EXE (read how the installer is produced: Installer/ and build_installer.ps1; it must embed exactly the verified candidate bundle; the candidates are in C:\ce_rc_scratch\c1056) into a clean throw-away profile with no Tim folders, then asserts: files placed where PackageContents.xml expects for each AutoCAD year folder layout, no write under Program Files or ProgramData unless documented, settings files created with Tim's defaults, uninstall/rollback works, the installer refuses an older version than approved (BUG-834) and warns. If the feature is disabled, make the script ready and state in the report what the desk must ask Tim to enable (an administrator step: do not do it). Also write a plain-English checklist of at most 20 steps for a human clean-PC dry run. Report C:\CE_PLAN\areas\CODEX_BUILD_SANDBOX_INSTALL_22OCT.md. This is a script-and-document job: no change to plugin source, no PR needed (commit only the script and report in C:\CE_PLAN).")
